    "field": "Paleoclimate modeling",
    "problem": "Understanding mid-Holocene climate is challenging because the distinct impacts of Arctic sea ice loss and solar insolation forcing are intertwined, and their separate contributions to past climate changes have not been clearly isolated.",
    "method": "This study performs idealized climate model perturbation experiments, including a mid-Holocene simulation where pre-industrial sea ice is maintained by increasing its albedo, to separate the climatic impacts of Arctic sea ice loss from those of direct insolation forcing.",
    "task": "The task is to isolate the climatic impacts of Arctic sea ice loss during the mid-Holocene, separating its effects from those of solar insolation forcing by using idealized climate model experiments.",
